    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1282">

                <pb facs="1320" n="1308" sameAs="frus:frus1945v08/pg1308"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867.24/7–545</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 55</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ankara</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-07-05">July 5,
                        1945</date>.<lb/>[Received July 18.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the Embassy’s telegrams no.
                    542, April 21, and no. 594, May 2, and to the Department’s telegram no. 562, May
                    26, 1945, I have the honor to enclose a copy of a note addressed by Sir Maurice
                    Drummond Peterson, the British Ambassador to Turkey, to the Acting Minister for
                    Foreign Affairs under date of June 30, 1945, regarding American Lend-Lease
                    material delivered to Turkey through British channels. The British note was sent
                    in accordance with new instructions received by the British Ambassador from the
                    Foreign Office in London, after ascertaining from Mr. Milton Winn, Special
                    Representative in Turkey of the Foreign Economic Administration and myself that
                    no objection was perceived to the note being sent.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwin</hi> C. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Wilson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>



                <xi:include href="d1282-a1.xml" xpointer="d1282-a1"/>
            </div>
